   "text": "I read the structure region by region and assembled the SMILES below. I assigned the stereochemistry from my reading of the wedges and hashes. Some of those were hard to tell apart in the drawing, notably the bond to the propoxy O and the methyl on the quaternary carbon next to it. Those two centres are therefore the least certain.\n\n**Macrocycle.** The ring runs: N(CH3), CH2, CH(CH3), CH2, C(CH3)(OPr), CH(O-sugar), CH(CH3), ketone C=O, quaternary C(CH3), lactone C(=O), ring O, CH2, and a CH that closes back to the N.\n\n**Substituents on the macrocycle.**\n- The CH next to the ring N carries a CH(OBn)CH2CH2CH3 side chain.\n- The quaternary carbon next to the ketone carries a CH3 and a CH2CH2N(CH3)CH2Ph chain.\n- The quaternary C(CH3) carries an O-propyl group.\n\n**Sugar.** The sugar is a desosamine-type pyranose. Going round the ring from the anomeric carbon, which bears the O-link to the macrocycle, the positions are:\n- C1: the glycosidic O\n- C2: OH\n- C3: N(CH3)2\n- C4: CH2\n- C5: CH(CH3)\n- the ring O closes back to C1\n\n**Stereochemistry.** The CH of the macrocycle attached to N has only plain bonds, so it has no stereo label. All other drawn wedge and hash centres are included.\n\nSMILES: CN1C[C@H](C)C[C@@](C)(OCCC)[C@H](O[C@@H]2O[C@H](C)C[C@H](N(C)C)[C@H]2O)[C@H](C)C(=O)[C@@](C)(CCN(C)Cc3ccccc3)C(=O)OCC1[C@H](OCc1ccccc1)CCC"
  }
